Actually, this would mean there's an extremely LOW probablility of your 
game lasting forever, because forever is so long that the probability of 
avoiding that 1.031E-8 continuously FOREVER drops off pretty fast.

It does mean your game will probably last an enormously long time. This 
actually raises the question, at what point will you get an overflow of 
some sort on the game length? Computers are finite devices, so it would 
be impossible for the game to last forever (at the very least, the 
hardware will break down). Then, what are the odds of the game lasting 
all the way until the overflow?

